          "sectionId": "sec_sample_1",
          "title": "1.1 Fundamental & Derived Quantities",
          "content": "Fundamental quantities are basic physical quantities that do not depend on any other quantities.\n\nExamples include length ($L$), mass ($M$), and time ($T$).\n\nDerived quantities are expressed from fundamental quantities, such as velocity ($v = \\frac{d}{t}$) and acceleration ($a = \\frac{v}{t}$).\n\nForce is given by Newton's second law: $$F = m \\cdot a = m \\frac{dv}{dt}$$",
